      "text": "We need to use the \"at least one card\" principle. So, the probability of the standard opposite event is given by:\n[(Number of possible outcomes - 1) / number of possible outcomes]³\n[(6 - 1) / 6]³ = (5/6)³ = 125/216\n\nThe probability of the standard opposite event is 125/216. Therefore, the probability that there are no identical numbers on all the dice is:\n\n1 - 125/216 = 91/216\n\nThe result is 91/216 expressed as a reduced fraction. Thus,\n\n[answer] = 91/216",
